  "notes": "LeanPi's own coding-capability ranking (PRD-024). Scores are on the documented 0-100 scale: 0-29 untrusted for multi-file edits; 30-49 single-file work; 50-69 the `quick` floor; 70-84 the `balanced` floor; 85-100 the `strong`/`review_strong` floor. Re-scoring a model is a normal revision; re-defining a band is a breaking change to every configured floor. Every record here is `evidence: estimated` because this repository records no PRD-021 benchmark run yet; promote a record to `measured` only alongside the run that produced the score. Prices are USD per million tokens on the 3:1 input:output blend, taken from the provider's published list price and not verified by this repository; null means unknown. A self-hosted model carries a real 0 monetary price (local compute is scored separately by the router), not an unknown one. A record is selectable only where the config declares its `model_id` or an alias as a `models.<role>.model` on an enabled backend; every other record is visible in /models but not routable, and `backend_hint` only picks the binding when the same model is declared on several backends. Update path: edit this file, bump `revision`, stamp `updated_at` on every touched record, note the change here. Revision 2 adds the CLI-backed models LeanPi discovers from the vendor CLIs (Claude aliases, the Codex catalog, OpenCode's list); their `coding_score` and `price_blended_per_mtok` are null until a PRD-021 run measures them, and each is its own record — never an alias across model generations.",
